80307200,11.4],[1682899200,8.9],[1685577600,0.5],[1688169600,8.3],[1690848000,9.9],[1693526400,2.7],[1696118400,9.3],[1698796800,-3.4],[1701388800,3.0],[1704067200,0.3],[1706745600,-3.2],[1709251200,5.2],[1711929600,-2.5],[1714521600,2.8],[1717200000,-1.0],[1719792000,-4.2],[1722470400,-4.4],[1725148800,2.2],[1727740800,2.8],[1730419200,0.6],[1733011200,-7.1],[1735689600,0.1],[1738368000,-2.1],[1740787200,-4.0],[1743465600,-2.7],[1746057600,-1.0],[1748736000,-0.9],[1751328000,0.5],[1754006400,-6.3],[1756684800,-0.3],[1759276800,-5.2],[1761955200,8.0],[1764547200,8.5],[1767225600,-2.3],[1769904000,-0.5],[1772323200,1.1]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the use-based IIP measure?","answer":"The Index of Industrial Production (IIP), compiled by MoSPI's National Statistics Office, tracks the volume of output of a fixed basket of industrial products. The use-based classification regroups the same items by how the goods are used: primary goods (basic inputs such as minerals, electricity-generation fuels, raw materials), capital goods (machinery and equipment used to produce other goods), intermediate goods (inputs used in further processing), infrastructure/construction goods (cement, steel products, paints, cables and similar), consumer durables and consumer non-durables.^Capital goods output is a read on investment demand, infrastructure/construction goods on building and public capex, and the two consumer groups on household demand, so the split is more informative for nowcasting than the headline."},{"question":"How should I read the index and the growth rate?","answer":"Index levels are relative to the base year average (=100), so 130 means 30 per cent above the base-year average. Levels are strongly seasonal (March is typically the peak, and the festive months move with Diwali timing), so use year-on-year growth, which compares the same month, for momentum. The growth rate here is the one published by MoSPI; the year-ago index for the early months of the new series is not published, so the published growth is shown instead of recomputing it.^Base effects matter: the quick estimate for a month is revised in the next two releases, so compare latest growth with caution."},{"question":"Definitions, revisions and caveats","answer":"This is the old series (base 2011-12=100); MoSPI replaced it with the 2022-23=100 series from the April 2026 data release, and it will not be updated. Levels of the two series are not comparable (MoSPI uses a linking factor to join them; none is applied here). Growth rates for the old series are those published at the time and may include later revisions.^Group weights differ between the old and new baskets, so shares and growth contributions are not comparable across the two records."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Discontinued base (2011-12=100); ends March 2026.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:22:54+00:00"}